{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/168738-no-game-no-life","id":168738,"title":"No Game No Life","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-14T02:40:05-07:00","id":168738,"title":"No Game No Life","content":"I really want to like this anime, the characters seem fun, and the setup is really interesting. But, the logic is already starting to break down for me, and I'm only on the second episode.<br /> <br /> See, the main guy challenges an ex-princess (it makes slightly more sense in context) to a game of rock-paper-scissors, with total domination of the losing party on the line. Ok, fair enough. She doesn't know rock-paper-scissors, being from another world, so he explains it to her. He then goes on to say that he will only play paper, and that if he plays anything else, he loses flat. So far, potentially interesting.<br /> <br /> This is followed by a three-minute sequence of her trying to out-think him, thinking what he will do, and adjusting accordingly. Finally, they throw, and: he wins! She played scissors, and he played...rock. Somehow, this results in him winning, <i>despite the fact that he clearly said that if he played anything other than paper, he loses</i>.<br /> <br /> Can someone please explain to me the logic of this exchange? Because it really, really doesn't hold to me: he said if he does something other than X, he loses. He did something other than X, so he wins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T02:48:42-07:00","id":168741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TM-G0bkl8MQ&amp;feature=kp\" data-code=\"TM-G0bkl8MQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/TM-G0bkl8MQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T03:02:48-07:00","id":168749,"title":"","content":"Helpful, thank you.<br /> <br /> The episode in question (it's the first half part) can be found <a href=\"http://http://www.gogoanime.com/no-game-no-life-episode-2\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> for those that are curious/want to review my logic. You don't really need to watch the first episode to get context, although it is moderately entertaining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 06-14-2014, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T03:35:07-07:00","id":168756,"title":"","content":"Sorry mate, I'm just... confused. I guess that counts as outsmarting her? Although, why would she go along with it if he lied to her face to win? Was she expecting it or something? I get the feeling something's being lost in translation here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T03:58:32-07:00","id":168760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/168738-no-game-no-life?p=168756#post168756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry mate, I'm just... confused. I guess that counts as outsmarting her? Although, why would she go along with it if he lied to her face to win? Was she expecting it or something? I get the feeling something's being lost in translation here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You and me both. Yet, as we see later, these things are mystically enforced, so it must have been legit. Except it clearly wasn't.<br /> <br /> I considered the translation solution, and I haven't ruled it out (because my Japanese is shaky at best), but it lines up with his gestures and stuff. I also considered he misled her, but since the favour he won was mystically enforced, which presumably couldn't happen if the laws of that universe were consistent. Since it's anime, it's very possible they're not, but if that's the case you can't have any actual tension.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I <i>want</i> to like this anime. But, either I'm missing a pretty basic logical step here, or the writing really is that bad. Hoping it's the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T12:54:39-07:00","id":170043,"title":"","content":"Ok, I haven't seen the show, but I went digging on some fan forums for the answer. I guess he wasn't trying to win in the first place. He wanted to maneuver her into a tie. He said if he chose anything other than paper he would lose, so she chose scissors, wanting to win. Then he chose rock, which beats scissors, so she lost, and he ALSO lost, since he didn't chose paper, so since they &quot;both lost&quot; that apparently made it a tie. I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T14:11:01-07:00","id":170107,"title":"","content":"I saw this show on crunchyroll and the gauge on my creep-dar nearly severed my carotid artery!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T02:17:12-07:00","id":170521,"title":"","content":"Not hard to follow. He plays rock, so he loses. But, his rock beats her scissors, so she also loses. So they both lose, which means it ends with a tie. He had already said that the rules of the game meant that, if there was a tie, she'd have to do something for him.<br /> <br /> So what that meant was, he'd basically &quot;win&quot; (get a favor from her) if he won the game, or if he tied with her. So he went for the tie.<br /> <br /> The whole point of the contest was to show the viewers that while the game itself is important, the rules that make the game are even more important. A good &quot;Rules Lawyer&quot; can finangle the rules of a game to create their own victory conditions, which is important later on in the show. The game, the rules and the psychology all play a major factor in determining victory, and if you set up the rules right, even if you &quot;lose&quot; you can still win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T07:02:50-07:00","id":170681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/168738-no-game-no-life?p=170107#post170107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw this show on crunchyroll and the gauge on my creep-dar nearly severed my carotid artery!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One wonders why you watched it then, let alone are commenting on this thread...<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/168738-no-game-no-life?p=170521#post170521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not hard to follow. He plays rock, so he loses. But, his rock beats her scissors, so she also loses. So they both lose, which means it ends with a tie. He had already said that the rules of the game meant that, if there was a tie, she'd have to do something for him.<br /> <br /> So what that meant was, he'd basically &quot;win&quot; (get a favor from her) if he won the game, or if he tied with her. So he went for the tie.<br /> <br /> The whole point of the contest was to show the viewers that while the game itself is important, the rules that make the game are even more important. A good &quot;Rules Lawyer&quot; can finangle the rules of a game to create their own victory conditions, which is important later on in the show. The game, the rules and the psychology all play a major factor in determining victory, and if you set up the rules right, even if you &quot;lose&quot; you can still win.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that makes sense. Forgot to take into account that lose-lose is also a tie, as well as same-same<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T23:20:16-07:00","id":173754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/168738-no-game-no-life?p=170681#post170681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One wonders why you watched it then, let alone are commenting on this thread...</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't know that it was so effed before I watched it. I'm commenting on this thread to throw my opinion hat into the ring as I think that critical discussion is important and that the attitude of 'if you don't like it keep walking' harms art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T02:12:46-07:00","id":173850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/168738-no-game-no-life?p=173754#post173754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't know that it was so effed before I watched it. I'm commenting on this thread to throw my opinion hat into the ring as I think that critical discussion is important and that the attitude of 'if you don't like it keep walking' harms art.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is that it, or are you just using that as a justification to sit and criticise something you don't like in a public forum to boost your ego?<br /> <br /> Your argument would hold water if your posts didn't frequently have a strongly antagonistic theme, which makes me think that you like to be antagonistic and justify it after the fact. Your clearly over-the-top classification and imagery is also far beyond constructive criticism (which, by the way, has to have a method of improving the work, not just saying &quot;it sucks&quot;, otherwise it's just complaining).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T07:25:06-07:00","id":174108,"title":"","content":"How would stating my opinion boost my ego, Allan? I haven't attacked your opinion; only shared my own experience, perhaps hoping to learn what people do enjoy about the show and rationalize my own viewing. In the interest of keeping things breezy (and reining in my straining ego) I'm prepared to drop the matter, but I really don't consider myself an antagonistic poster. Perhaps I need to work on my tone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}